WEBVTT


00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.921
MAX: it was my fault.
l was the one driving when it happened.


00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:11.481
After the accident, l started seeing things,
things that couldn't be real.


00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:12.921
But l'm not crazy.


00:01:13.222 --> 00:01:16.222
{GLASS SHUTTERING}


00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.761
l know.


00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.281
Your father knows.


00:01:22.401 --> 00:01:24.361
Anyone who knows you knows that.


00:01:26.761 --> 00:01:31.041
Look, Max, l've seen you every day
for the past two months.


00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:36.281
Maybe you're starting to let go
of your misplaced guilt.


00:01:36.401 --> 00:01:40.161
Maybe you're ready to stop blaming
yourself for what happened.


00:01:41.681 --> 00:01:44.521
But there's no one else to blame.


00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.201
it’s gotten to the point
where l look in the mirror...


00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.001
and l'm not even sure
what's real anymore.


00:05:53.921 --> 00:05:55.321
Fancy mirror.


00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:14.001
Later.


00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:21.601
You're a lady-killer, Schow.


00:06:22.241 --> 00:06:23.801
Lady-killer.


00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:02.881
What's going' on?


00:07:03.001 --> 00:07:05.481
Hey! What-


00:07:07.082 --> 00:07:10.982
{SCREAMING}


00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:17.681
No!


00:07:33.082 --> 00:07:38.082
{SCREAMING LOUDLY}


00:08:00.083 --> 00:08:05.083
{CONTINUE SCREAMING LOUDLY}


00:08:24.361 --> 00:08:25.401
Yeah.


00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:26.681
Max.


00:08:26.801 --> 00:08:29.681
- Who's this?
- Are you still sleeping? What time is it?


00:08:29.801 --> 00:08:32.481
- Dad? Is that you?
- Of course it's me.


00:08:32.601 --> 00:08:34.401
Yeah. Is everything all right?


00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:37.721
Yeah. Did l wake you up?
You don't sound good.


00:08:37.841 --> 00:08:40.761
- l'm fine. l'must getting some sleep.
- Thank you.


00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:42.201
Careful over there.


00:08:42.321 --> 00:08:45.121
Just getting to the point where l can
sleep through the night again.


00:08:45.241 --> 00:08:47.361
Good, good.
You gotta get your rest.


00:08:47.481 --> 00:08:49.601
- Keller.
- Yeah?


00:08:49.721 --> 00:08:52.601
- Five minutes.
- Okay, that's great.


00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:58.121
That is the Mayflower
signature right there.


00:08:58.961 --> 00:09:00.841
That glass has been through so much.


00:09:00.961 --> 00:09:02.921
You can see the care
that went into making it.


00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.921
Even the base came
from the original store.


00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:09.281
So that gives us the- its spirit.


00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.641
l think it's perfect.


00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:14.761
Look, Max, for the last two months
the police have been all over us...


00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:16.841
looking for that missing girl.


00:09:16.961 --> 00:09:20.161
Max, we may not be able
to open on time.


00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.041
Really? l didn't know that, Dad.


00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.881
And then last week
our night security guard goes crazy.


00:09:25.001 --> 00:09:27.321
He cuts himself up bad and he quits.


00:09:28.241 --> 00:09:31.921
Max, l've got weeks of work to do
and mo weeks out from opening.


00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.001
The last thing l need to be doing...


00:09:34.121 --> 00:09:36.081
is looking for a new night watchman.


00:09:36.201 --> 00:09:39.961
l'm just not sure l'm ready yet, Dad,
after all that's happened this year and-


00:09:40.081 --> 00:09:42.721
Max. This is what you need.


00:09:42.841 --> 00:09:45.281
And, honestly,
right now l need you, Max.


00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.841
l know it'll help you
take your mind off things.


00:09:47.961 --> 00:09:49.601
- Yeah.
- Look.


00:09:49.721 --> 00:09:53.081
- l think it's goanna be good.
- All right, Dad. l'll do it.


00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:56.241
Thanks for the opportunity.


00:09:56.361 --> 00:10:00.001
No, no, no, thank you, Max.
l tell you what.


00:10:00.121 --> 00:10:03.561
Why don't you come in to work
a little early and find me...


00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:06.641
so that we can say hello
before you clock in. Okay?


00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.801
- Yeah. Sure. l'll come find you.
- All right.


00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.761
- We'll see you in a little bit.
- Okay, Dad.


00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.841
- Bye.
- Bye-bye.


00:10:36.841 --> 00:10:38.441
Shoot.


00:10:48.201 --> 00:10:49.521
l got it.


00:10:51.081 --> 00:10:53.041
Just trying to help.


00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:04.201
That may or may not be the case...


00:11:04.321 --> 00:11:08.441
but you should put that on your punch list,
then take care of that first thing tomorrow.


00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:09.521
Would you do that?


00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:13.881
Jenna, will you take care
of the accessories? That'll be great.


00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:20.321
Ladies and gentlemen, the thing
l am most proud of in the entire store.


00:11:20.441 --> 00:11:22.881
- This is my son Max.
- Hi.


00:11:23.001 --> 00:11:24.641
- How are you, son?
- Good.


00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:26.321
Yeah? Get some rest?


00:11:26.441 --> 00:11:28.241
- Yeah.
- Okay.


00:11:28.361 --> 00:11:30.121
l wanna introduce you
to a few people.


00:11:30.241 --> 00:11:31.681
This is Keller Landreaux.


00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:34.521
He's goanna be our store manager
when we open in a few weeks.


00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:37.801
Keller told us that we could buy
property down here in New Orleans...


00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.721
for a song and a dime.


00:11:39.841 --> 00:11:42.961
That's exactly what we did.
Smart man.


00:11:43.081 --> 00:11:44.721
Glad to meet you, Max.


00:11:44.841 --> 00:11:47.521
My pleasure.
Thanks for having me.


00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:50.721
And this beautiful young lady
we have right here...


00:11:50.841 --> 00:11:53.121
this is Jenna McCarty.


00:11:53.241 --> 00:11:55.001
Jenna is the head buyer
for the store...


00:11:55.121 --> 00:11:58.081
and she has promised to bring us
a little bit of that Fifth Avenue flair...


00:11:58.201 --> 00:11:59.801
to Bourbon Street, yes?


00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:02.121
Sure.
Nice to meet you, Max.


00:12:02.241 --> 00:12:03.201
You too.


00:12:03.321 --> 00:12:06.961
You know, Max,
Ladies love a man in uniform.


00:12:07.081 --> 00:12:12.481
Yeah, Dad, l'm sure the polyester pants
really help seal the deal.


00:12:13.721 --> 00:12:17.561
And last but not least
l'd like to introduce you to Ryan P-


00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:19.321
- What was your last name?
- Parker.


00:12:19.441 --> 00:12:22.641
l'm just kidding you. Ryan Parker,
our vice president in charge of operations.


00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.601
- Good to meet you, Max.
- Likewise.


00:12:24.721 --> 00:12:28.441
While you're out there on your rounds,
you see something that doesn't look right...


00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.641
you got a problem
with plumbing or electric, fire...


00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:35.361
you get a candy bar stuck
in the vending machine, you call Ryan.


00:12:35.481 --> 00:12:37.841
That's after you call me.


00:12:39.481 --> 00:12:43.041
Listen. l'm goanna let you go.
l know you got a job to do.


00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:46.481
And we need to continue on our rounds.
Good luck out there.


00:12:46.601 --> 00:12:48.161
- Thanks, Dad.
- All right.


00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:50.081
Shall we?


00:14:05.082 --> 00:14:08.082
{SCREAMING}


00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.921
You all right?


00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.201
Sorry. First night.


00:14:27.721 --> 00:14:31.401
So, Max, you say you've been
having those visions again?


00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:32.761
Yeah.


00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:38.121
Were you taking drugs or had you been
drinking when you had this episode?


00:14:38.241 --> 00:14:42.201
No. It was last night at my new job.


00:14:42.321 --> 00:14:46.921
l saw a woman
in one of the mirrors at my work.


00:14:47.721 --> 00:14:49.881
You saw a woman?


00:14:50.001 --> 00:14:53.201
Yeah. She was looking back at me
from the other side.


00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:57.641
Her reflection looked like a corpse.


00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:01.921
She probably reminded you
of Kayla in some way.


00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:05.521
Your mind's way of
processing the mental shock.


00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:08.521
And the pills l prescribed?


00:15:09.201 --> 00:15:11.601
Yeah, l took one.


00:15:11.721 --> 00:15:13.841
- That's all?
- Yeah.


00:15:13.961 --> 00:15:14.921
Good.


00:15:15.721 --> 00:15:18.561
l wanted to take more,
but l decided not to.


00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.321
Very good.


00:15:20.441 --> 00:15:22.801
So should we put
the straitjacket on me now...


00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.161
or should we wait until my time's up?


00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:27.521
l'm not worried about you, Max.


00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:29.401
- No?
- Not at all.


00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:32.601
What you're telling me,
it's a good thing.


00:15:32.721 --> 00:15:33.721
Yeah?


00:15:34.441 --> 00:15:38.681
These representations of Kayla,
hallucinations or not...


00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:42.561
are a sign that you're starting
to get your life back in order...


00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:48.121
that maybe you're starting to let go of
your misplaced guilt about her death...


00:15:48.241 --> 00:15:51.961
that you're ready to stop blaming yourself
for what happened.


00:15:53.081 --> 00:15:54.561
What intrigues me...


00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.881
is that now that you've stopped wallowing
in the drugs and the alcohol...


00:15:58.001 --> 00:16:00.041
now that you're sober...


00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:03.961
your mind is ready to begin
processing the tragedy in earnest.


00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:09.561
You wanna come see me again
next week...


00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.441
get back to a regular
appointment type thing?


00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.521
Sure.


00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:47.201
Yeah.
l'll run the numbers tomorrow.


00:16:47.321 --> 00:16:49.801
Okay. And then l placed the orders
for size 8 through 12.


00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:52.121
- No. No!
- Why? But-


00:16:52.241 --> 00:16:56.161
it’s like l told you earlier. l don't
want to order any of the larger sizes.


00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.641
But l don't-
Why, Jenna?


00:16:57.760 --> 00:16:58.721
Why?


00:16:58.841 --> 00:17:02.081
Because this Mayflower has to convey
the message that it's a boutique.


00:17:02.201 --> 00:17:04.681
And boutique
implies skin and bones.


00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:07.921
Yeah, l'm really sure.
Right, right. Okay.


00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.841
So, if we do the research...


00:17:09.961 --> 00:17:12.521
and it shows that the demographic
is full of heifers...


00:17:12.641 --> 00:17:14.401
then we'll order accordingly.


00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:17.961
But listen to me- Until then, four is
the new eight. Do you understand me?


00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:20.881
- Yeah, l got it.
- Thank you. Talk to you later.


00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:23.241
Camera in the bathroom?


00:19:30.681 --> 00:19:32.801
Henry, you dirty dog.


00:19:38.721 --> 00:19:40.681
Just want to check in
on my new favourite employee.


00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:43.521
l'm good. Just happy to be here,
Mr. Landreaux.


00:19:43.641 --> 00:19:45.401
We're happy to have you, Max.


00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:49.721
Your dad entrusted me with the opening
of the new Mayflower as my top priority.


00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:53.961
You seem committed,
being here so late.


00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:57.521
Yeah. l can't let anything
interfere with our grand opening.


00:19:57.641 --> 00:20:00.081
Yeah. l should do my rounds.


00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:03.521
Hey, Max,
will you do me a favour?


00:20:03.641 --> 00:20:07.001
Call me Keller.
We're all family here at the Mayflower.


00:20:08.441 --> 00:20:10.361
Okay.


00:22:20.600 --> 00:22:21.761
Jenna?


00:22:22.401 --> 00:22:24.201
What are you-


00:22:33.120 --> 00:22:34.081
No!


00:22:59.641 --> 00:23:01.001
Fuck.


00:24:25.280 --> 00:24:27.201
Morning', rookie.


00:24:27.320 --> 00:24:29.321
So, how did that last night go?


00:24:33.080 --> 00:24:35.281
Everything all right?


00:24:55.481 --> 00:24:57.041
Dr. Beaumont's office.


00:24:57.161 --> 00:25:00.681
This is Max Matheson. l need to see
Dr. Beaumont as soon as possible.


00:25:00.800 --> 00:25:02.561
Okay, let me see what l have.


00:25:10.320 --> 00:25:12.481
How do you think this happened?


00:25:12.600 --> 00:25:14.521
l don't know.


00:25:15.800 --> 00:25:19.281
Looks more like a-
just a terrible accident...


00:25:19.401 --> 00:25:21.401
but maybe someone killed her.


00:25:22.040 --> 00:25:25.121
Homicide by handmade guillotine?


00:25:25.241 --> 00:25:27.601
That would impress even yours truly.


00:25:27.721 --> 00:25:29.841
Yeah, me too, Pete.


00:25:29.961 --> 00:25:31.321
Me too.


00:25:43.201 --> 00:25:45.161
- Dr. Beaumont?
- Yes?


00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:51.401
Do you really believe all that, your
explanation for what's happening to me?


00:25:51.520 --> 00:25:55.241
Well, of course.
There's really no other explanation.


00:25:55.360 --> 00:25:58.161
And the fact that it's
all related to the mirrors...


00:25:58.280 --> 00:26:00.321
that that's how
l'm seeing these visions?


00:26:01.201 --> 00:26:02.561
Reconnaissance.


00:26:02.681 --> 00:26:04.041
What's that?


00:26:04.161 --> 00:26:08.921
it’s a French term from Jacques Lacan's
mirror stage of psychoanalytic theory.


00:26:09.040 --> 00:26:11.401
The ego is a product
of false reflections.


00:26:12.360 --> 00:26:13.281
Reconnaissance-


00:26:13.441 --> 00:26:17.721
when the subject is alienated
from his or her self.


00:26:20.001 --> 00:26:21.521
in English?


00:26:21.641 --> 00:26:24.121
Nobody sees anything in a mirror...


00:26:24.241 --> 00:26:26.801
that isn't simply a part of them...


00:26:26.921 --> 00:26:29.521
not even things
they think they're seeing.


00:26:29.641 --> 00:26:33.321
Every culture has its own particular
myth set regarding mirrors.


00:26:33.441 --> 00:26:35.361
in Korea, for example...


00:26:35.481 --> 00:26:39.881
it's believed that a person's soul
can be trapped inside of a mirror...


00:26:40.001 --> 00:26:41.841
as it leaves the body.


00:26:41.961 --> 00:26:46.241
You've heard the old adage, a cracked
mirror brings seven years bad luck.


00:26:46.360 --> 00:26:49.121
And even here
in the South's recent past...


00:26:49.241 --> 00:26:52.801
it was not uncommon to cover
all of the mirrors in a house...


00:26:52.921 --> 00:26:55.641
where the wake of a deceased person
was being held.


00:26:55.760 --> 00:26:58.561
There's even a clinical diagnosis...


00:26:58.681 --> 00:27:02.601
for an intense fear of mirrors
called spectrophobia.


00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:06.681
Lots of psychic baggage
in them there mirrors.


00:27:06.800 --> 00:27:09.281
So l guess
l'm doing pretty well, then?


00:27:09.401 --> 00:27:10.761
in light of all you've been through...


00:27:10.881 --> 00:27:13.761
combined with all the superstitions
we hold regarding mirrors...


00:27:13.881 --> 00:27:17.361
l'd say you're doing
pretty good indeed.


00:28:09.800 --> 00:28:11.521
How are you holding' up?


00:28:14.520 --> 00:28:16.081
Fine.


00:28:17.161 --> 00:28:19.041
Your father didn't tell you.


00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:21.601
Tell me what?


00:28:21.721 --> 00:28:24.801
Jenna McCarty,
the woman you met the other day...


00:28:24.921 --> 00:28:27.161
she died last night.


00:28:27.280 --> 00:28:29.321
They found her in her apartment.


00:28:31.600 --> 00:28:33.281
How did she die?


00:28:33.401 --> 00:28:35.681
The police said she fell through glass.


00:28:35.800 --> 00:28:38.201
it ripped her head off.


00:28:38.320 --> 00:28:40.241
it was a horrible accident.


00:28:41.681 --> 00:28:43.681
Such a tragedy.


00:28:46.040 --> 00:28:48.041
Are you all right?


00:28:48.961 --> 00:28:53.201
Yeah. l'm... just surprised.


00:28:54.481 --> 00:28:56.121
You sure?


00:28:56.241 --> 00:28:57.601
Yeah.


00:28:58.360 --> 00:29:01.001
- Will you call me if you need anything?
- Yeah.


00:29:02.881 --> 00:29:03.801
Thanks.


00:29:04.921 --> 00:29:06.881
l still can't believe it.


00:29:38.800 --> 00:29:39.961
Hello?


00:29:45.280 --> 00:29:47.241
Are you here? It's me.


00:30:01.161 --> 00:30:02.641
Hello?


00:30:08.600 --> 00:30:10.481
Oh, God.


00:30:10.600 --> 00:30:13.361
l'm really starting to lose it again.


00:32:40.062 --> 00:32:43.962
{SCREAMING}


00:33:29.080 --> 00:33:31.361
''P.'' ''P.'' Parker.


00:33:57.062 --> 00:34:00.762
{SCREAMING}


00:34:36.841 --> 00:34:38.121
Where's the number?


00:34:48.122 --> 00:34:51.822
{PHONE RINGING}


00:34:52.001 --> 00:34:52.961
God!


00:35:06.520 --> 00:35:10.481
Oh, God!
{SCREAMING}


00:35:26.080 --> 00:35:27.921
Hi. You've reached Ryan's
answering machine.


00:35:28.040 --> 00:35:30.081
l'm unable to get up
and get the phone right now...


00:35:30.200 --> 00:35:32.761
so leave me a message with your name
and your phone number...


00:35:32.881 --> 00:35:35.201
- Come on, goddamn it.
- and l will get back to you shortly.


00:35:35.321 --> 00:35:36.721
Take care.


00:36:05.022 --> 00:36:08.722
NO,NO!


00:36:30.023 --> 00:36:32.023
{SCREAMING LOUDLY}


00:36:56.160 --> 00:36:58.561
You ever seen a 10-56 like that?


00:36:58.680 --> 00:37:00.321
l'm not sure.


00:37:01.321 --> 00:37:02.441
One thing l know-


00:37:02.560 --> 00:37:05.281
This is the second death of an employee
who worked at the Mayflower.


00:37:05.401 --> 00:37:08.481
The third, if you count the girl
who went missing two months ago.


00:37:21.401 --> 00:37:23.201
- Officer.
- Yes, sir.


00:37:23.321 --> 00:37:25.801
The witnesses.
Where'd you put 'em?


00:37:29.281 --> 00:37:30.521
Hey, Pic.


00:37:33.001 --> 00:37:35.001
Check out the badge.


00:37:41.040 --> 00:37:44.041
He's definitely a person of interest.


00:37:59.640 --> 00:38:00.761
Hello?


00:38:00.881 --> 00:38:02.801
Yeah, hi, Dad.


00:38:04.921 --> 00:38:06.881
What time is it?


00:38:07.001 --> 00:38:09.041
l don't know. It's late.


00:38:11.720 --> 00:38:13.281
What's going on, Max?


00:38:13.401 --> 00:38:16.801
l'm just- l'm calling
to let you know that l'm-


00:38:16.921 --> 00:38:19.721
l'm goanna be quitting my job.


00:38:20.640 --> 00:38:21.961
Are you all right?


00:38:22.080 --> 00:38:24.161
No, not really.


00:38:26.001 --> 00:38:28.241
l can't keep working there.


00:38:29.881 --> 00:38:31.801
it’s too much.


00:38:32.441 --> 00:38:34.001
Too much?


00:38:34.120 --> 00:38:37.241
Yeah.
l think l'm seeing things again.


00:38:37.361 --> 00:38:39.201
l'm really sorry.


00:38:39.321 --> 00:38:41.121
l don't care about the job.
Just-


00:38:41.240 --> 00:38:44.601
- l need to know that you're okay.
- Yeah.


00:38:47.001 --> 00:38:48.401
l'm okay.


00:38:52.120 --> 00:38:57.361
Stop by tomorrow and drop off
your ID badge and all that, you know.


00:38:58.001 --> 00:39:01.441
Yeah, l will.
Thank you for understanding, Dad.


00:39:01.560 --> 00:39:04.201
Max, l'm your father...


00:39:04.321 --> 00:39:06.041
and l do support you.


00:39:06.160 --> 00:39:07.361
You know that.


00:39:07.481 --> 00:39:09.121
Yeah, l do.


00:39:09.240 --> 00:39:10.721
Okay.


00:39:10.841 --> 00:39:12.481
Get some rest.


00:39:12.600 --> 00:39:13.681
Okay.


00:40:40.361 --> 00:40:42.561
What's wrong with you?


00:41:29.080 --> 00:41:30.321
Dad!


00:41:37.841 --> 00:41:39.601
Dad!


00:41:41.401 --> 00:41:43.361
Max, what are you doing here?


00:41:44.080 --> 00:41:46.481
l know what l need to do.


00:41:48.441 --> 00:41:49.641
l came by-


00:41:51.040 --> 00:41:53.961
- l changed my mind.
- Good for you.


00:41:54.080 --> 00:41:56.241
l wanna stay at the Mayflower.


00:41:56.361 --> 00:41:58.921
Come here.
Give me one.


00:42:00.281 --> 00:42:02.081
Thank you.


00:42:02.200 --> 00:42:03.881
it’s goanna be okay.


00:42:04.640 --> 00:42:06.321
Yeah, l know.


00:42:07.761 --> 00:42:10.001
We don't know why things happen
the way that they do...


00:42:10.120 --> 00:42:13.441
but they have a tendency
to work themselves out.


00:42:13.560 --> 00:42:15.761
Everything happens for a reason, Max.


00:42:15.881 --> 00:42:17.601
Yeah. Right.


00:42:22.801 --> 00:42:24.721
Are you hungry?


00:42:27.040 --> 00:42:28.761
Want a slice?


00:42:28.881 --> 00:42:30.801
l'm good.


00:42:37.881 --> 00:42:41.441
- Can you hold up a sec?
- Just need a minute.


00:42:42.361 --> 00:42:44.201
May l help you?


00:42:46.361 --> 00:42:48.481
Detective Huston, Homicide.


00:42:48.600 --> 00:42:51.121
Detective Piccalilli.
What he said.


00:42:52.120 --> 00:42:53.481
Homicide?


00:42:53.600 --> 00:42:55.561
We just come by to ask you
a few questions...


00:42:55.680 --> 00:42:57.641
about some fellow employees
at the Mayflower...


00:42:57.761 --> 00:43:01.001
see if you might know anything about 'em
that might be of interest to us.


00:43:01.120 --> 00:43:02.641
We went by your house.


00:43:02.761 --> 00:43:04.201
You weren't there.


00:43:05.720 --> 00:43:07.841
Okay. And?


00:43:07.961 --> 00:43:10.721
And why don't you tell us.


00:43:11.841 --> 00:43:13.001
Tell you what?


00:43:13.120 --> 00:43:16.561
You heard about one
Miss Jenna McCarty, correct?


00:43:18.321 --> 00:43:19.281
Yes.


00:43:19.401 --> 00:43:21.321
And you were also at the home...


00:43:22.040 --> 00:43:25.881
of Mr. Ryan Parker earlier tonight,
weren't you?


00:43:27.321 --> 00:43:29.441
Yeah. But-


00:43:29.560 --> 00:43:32.161
Then certainly you must have
gathered that he was dead, right?


00:43:32.281 --> 00:43:33.401
Right.


00:43:33.520 --> 00:43:36.201
Brutally murdered, as a matter of fact.


00:43:36.321 --> 00:43:38.041
Hence, homicide.


00:43:39.001 --> 00:43:40.841
Plural, actually, Pic.


00:43:40.961 --> 00:43:43.721
Homicides, with an S.


00:43:43.841 --> 00:43:45.401
You're right, man.


00:43:45.520 --> 00:43:47.721
There've been two homicides...


00:43:47.841 --> 00:43:50.161
involving employees
of the Mayflower this week.


00:43:50.281 --> 00:43:52.241
Since you were
at the scene of the crime tonight-


00:43:52.361 --> 00:43:53.761
And in charge of security-


00:43:53.881 --> 00:43:58.001
it stands to reason that you might have
an opinion or two about these matters.


00:44:03.080 --> 00:44:04.601
Am l a suspect?


00:44:09.520 --> 00:44:10.921
No.


00:44:11.040 --> 00:44:13.201
- Not yet.
- Not yet?


00:44:13.321 --> 00:44:14.561
Not officially.


00:44:15.520 --> 00:44:17.441
What, not officially?


00:44:17.560 --> 00:44:20.001
At this point the only thing
you're suspected of...


00:44:20.120 --> 00:44:22.281
is being a lousy security guard.


00:44:25.281 --> 00:44:30.601
So, why were you out front
of the deceased's home earlier tonight?


00:44:30.720 --> 00:44:34.041
Kind of a creepy coincidence,
don't you think?


00:44:35.720 --> 00:44:36.921
No.


00:44:37.841 --> 00:44:41.041
l don't think
it was a creepy coincidence.


00:44:41.160 --> 00:44:42.761
Not at all.


00:44:42.881 --> 00:44:46.481
And l might be a lousy security guard,
but it seems to me that the two of you are...


00:44:46.600 --> 00:44:50.681
not too much better
at the detective stuff.


00:44:50.801 --> 00:44:52.961
lf you'd have done your homework,
you would've seen that...


00:44:53.080 --> 00:44:55.401
Mr. Parker is
the vice president of operations...


00:44:55.520 --> 00:44:58.601
here at this particular branch
of the Mayflower Department Store.


00:44:58.720 --> 00:45:02.281
And per protocol,
if anything goes wrong, it is my duty...


00:45:02.401 --> 00:45:05.121
to contact Mr. Parker immediately.


00:45:05.240 --> 00:45:07.081
Why not just call him?


00:45:07.200 --> 00:45:10.081
As soon as you stop badgering me
and you get back to your work...


00:45:10.200 --> 00:45:13.401
you'll be happy to see that the phone
records indicate that l did, in fact...


00:45:13.520 --> 00:45:15.801
try to call Mr. Parker.


00:45:15.921 --> 00:45:20.281
Probably, l might add, during the time at
which Mr. Parker was being, as you say...


00:45:20.401 --> 00:45:22.321
brutally murdered.


00:45:24.120 --> 00:45:27.841
Might be kind of hard for me
to have been the one killing him too.


00:45:27.961 --> 00:45:32.241
So you ran over
to the deceased's home...


00:45:32.361 --> 00:45:35.561
to let him know you were
having a problem with-


00:45:35.680 --> 00:45:37.641
With the mirrors.


00:45:43.600 --> 00:45:47.521
So unless there are any other questions,
l'd really like to get back to my work.


00:45:47.640 --> 00:45:50.081
- No more questions.
- For now.


00:45:50.200 --> 00:45:53.241
- We just wanted to stop by.
- Say hi.


00:45:53.361 --> 00:45:56.161
And let you know that
we got our eye out on you.


00:45:59.240 --> 00:46:02.361
l feel so much safer knowing that.


00:46:02.481 --> 00:46:04.561
Thank you very much, Detectives.


00:46:21.240 --> 00:46:23.121
l don't understand.


00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:34.041
Who are you?


00:46:36.160 --> 00:46:38.161
What do you want?


00:48:00.520 --> 00:48:02.401
She worked here.


00:49:48.841 --> 00:49:52.521
- Hello?
- Hi. Is this Elizabeth Reigns?


00:50:02.200 --> 00:50:03.641
Hi. Elizabeth.


00:50:04.441 --> 00:50:06.561
Hi. l'm Max.


00:50:06.680 --> 00:50:08.001
Hi.


00:50:11.640 --> 00:50:15.041
You wanna talk about my sister?
You said you might have some information.


00:50:15.160 --> 00:50:16.721
Yeah.


00:50:18.200 --> 00:50:22.561
l think maybe l've seen her recently.


00:50:23.560 --> 00:50:24.921
Where?


00:50:26.001 --> 00:50:28.161
At the Mayflower.


00:50:28.281 --> 00:50:30.401
Where at the Mayflower?


00:50:32.841 --> 00:50:34.721
in the mirrors.


00:50:36.881 --> 00:50:40.081
What- In the mirrors?
What do you mean, in the mirrors?


00:50:40.200 --> 00:50:42.321
Yeah, l know it sounds crazy...


00:50:42.441 --> 00:50:46.081
but l see her reflection
in the mirrors.


00:50:46.200 --> 00:50:50.801
And l-
Then l turn around and she's gone.


00:50:50.921 --> 00:50:53.081
She's not there anymore.


00:50:54.120 --> 00:50:56.081
l don't know
who put you up to this.


00:50:56.200 --> 00:50:59.681
My sister, my little sister Eleanor has
been missing for almost two months now.


00:50:59.801 --> 00:51:01.961
And you just turn this
into some kind of joke.


00:51:03.921 --> 00:51:06.161
No, it's not a joke.


00:51:07.600 --> 00:51:09.121
Listen to me.


00:51:09.240 --> 00:51:11.201
- Listen, l'm serious.
- Don't touch me!


00:51:12.881 --> 00:51:15.121
Just don't touch me.


00:51:15.240 --> 00:51:18.041
l know what l said, it sounds crazy.


00:51:19.881 --> 00:51:21.761
it’s the truth.


00:51:23.640 --> 00:51:27.561
So this started happening the first night
that you were working there?


00:51:29.321 --> 00:51:30.841
How can that be?


00:51:30.961 --> 00:51:32.921
How is it that out of everyone
that works there...


00:51:33.040 --> 00:51:35.561
you're the only one
that can see my sister?


00:51:36.761 --> 00:51:40.721
A year ago,
l was driving with my fiancée.


00:52:01.281 --> 00:52:02.321
What?


00:52:03.160 --> 00:52:04.521
Nothing'.


00:52:07.401 --> 00:52:08.761
Okay.


00:52:13.401 --> 00:52:16.401
Can you reach into the backpack,
grab my phone for me?


00:52:16.520 --> 00:52:19.161
- Yeah.
- l need to call my dad.


00:52:19.281 --> 00:52:21.881
Okay, hang on. Drive safe.


00:52:22.001 --> 00:52:24.681
- Okay, Max?
- Yeah. l got it.


00:52:24.801 --> 00:52:26.561
- Please. Thank you.
- l can see.


00:52:26.680 --> 00:52:28.281
Perfectly?


00:52:28.401 --> 00:52:31.361
- Come on, l'm a great driver.
- Yeah.


00:52:31.481 --> 00:52:32.441
Okay.


00:52:34.200 --> 00:52:36.001
Where did you say it was?


00:52:36.881 --> 00:52:38.041
in the front there.


00:52:39.281 --> 00:52:41.641
Front. Front.


00:52:42.841 --> 00:52:45.641
- Are you sure?
- Honey, it's right there.


00:52:54.361 --> 00:52:56.401
Any luck?


00:52:58.720 --> 00:53:00.081
Oh, my God.


00:53:01.001 --> 00:53:04.121
Max Matheson,
is this what l think it is?


00:53:04.240 --> 00:53:07.201
- Well, what do you think it is?
- l don't know.


00:53:36.921 --> 00:53:38.921
A drunk driver.


00:53:39.040 --> 00:53:40.801
He hit you?


00:53:40.921 --> 00:53:42.881
l swerved to avoid him.


00:53:43.001 --> 00:53:45.961
l wrapped my car
around a telephone fall.


00:53:46.080 --> 00:53:48.441
Technically, it was my fault.


00:53:50.240 --> 00:53:52.081
And your fiancée, she-


00:53:52.921 --> 00:53:55.281
she died in the accident?


00:53:57.120 --> 00:53:59.001
We both did.


00:55:50.441 --> 00:55:51.801
Start an IV.


00:55:57.560 --> 00:55:59.121
Stay still, sir.


00:56:04.761 --> 00:56:06.761
They brought you back.


00:56:09.441 --> 00:56:11.841
Maybe l brought back
something with me...


00:56:11.961 --> 00:56:16.121
some ability to see
the other side or something.


00:56:20.321 --> 00:56:23.601
Afterward, l just got pretty
screwed up for a while-


00:56:23.720 --> 00:56:25.281
drugs, alcohol...


00:56:25.401 --> 00:56:27.361
whatever l could put into me.


00:56:28.680 --> 00:56:31.121
Like l was trying to get
closer to her or something.


00:56:32.200 --> 00:56:34.721
- Wasn't your fault.
- l was the one driving.


00:56:34.841 --> 00:56:38.121
You were trying to swerve to get out
of the way. You were trying to save her.


00:56:39.441 --> 00:56:42.001
Yeah, but l couldn't.


00:56:43.961 --> 00:56:46.121
l couldn't save her.


00:56:46.240 --> 00:56:48.761
You wanted to see her again.


00:56:49.921 --> 00:56:52.001
Yeah. More than you could ever know.


00:56:58.761 --> 00:57:00.881
How long's your sister been missing?


00:57:02.240 --> 00:57:04.681
About two months.


00:57:05.801 --> 00:57:07.841
And you still think she's-


00:57:09.761 --> 00:57:11.201
Dead?


00:57:16.120 --> 00:57:20.521
Of course, the cops say that young women
up and leave all the time to start new lives.


00:57:23.441 --> 00:57:25.281
But Eleanor and l...


00:57:25.401 --> 00:57:29.881
we weren't just sisters, we were
best friends, we were soul mates.


00:57:30.001 --> 00:57:31.921
And the night that she...


00:57:32.040 --> 00:57:34.481
disappeared...


00:57:34.600 --> 00:57:39.121
l woke up from a deep sleep,
screaming for no reason.


00:57:40.240 --> 00:57:44.041
My heart was beating so fast,
l thought it was goanna explode.


00:57:45.600 --> 00:57:47.561
l knew right then and there.


00:57:49.520 --> 00:57:52.961
What was your sister doing
the day she disappeared?


00:57:53.600 --> 00:57:55.841
Working at the Mayflower.


00:57:55.961 --> 00:58:01.001
There was some sort of party that night
and she was- she'd just been hired on.


00:58:01.120 --> 00:58:04.081
They were having
a groundbreaking celebration.


00:58:14.680 --> 00:58:17.601
l gotta get to work.


00:58:17.720 --> 00:58:21.321
Yeah, l gotta get some sleep.
l gotta work again tonight.


00:58:21.441 --> 00:58:24.081
Call me if anything else comes up.


00:58:25.120 --> 00:58:26.841
Absolutely.


00:58:26.961 --> 00:58:29.041
Thank you, Max.


00:58:31.240 --> 00:58:34.641
l haven't done anything.
Not yet, anyway.


00:58:34.761 --> 00:58:37.121
But you're trying.


00:58:37.240 --> 00:58:40.121
That's more than anyone else
has been willing to do around here.


00:59:22.200 --> 00:59:24.201
Eleanor.


00:59:26.921 --> 00:59:29.081
l'm tying my best.


00:59:29.200 --> 00:59:31.481
l'm tying my best. Really.


00:59:37.441 --> 00:59:41.041
Please. Stop doing this.


00:59:46.560 --> 00:59:48.721
Wait. What are you doing?


00:59:50.481 --> 00:59:53.921
Please, don't- don't do this.


00:59:54.040 --> 00:59:56.161
Please.


00:59:56.281 --> 00:59:57.641
No.


00:59:57.761 --> 01:00:02.281
Tell me what l need to do.
Please, tell me. Just-


01:00:02.401 --> 01:00:04.561
What is it? What?


01:00:34.160 --> 01:00:35.481
Hello.


01:00:36.520 --> 01:00:38.561
What night did she disappear?


01:00:38.680 --> 01:00:40.441
it was a Wednesday night.


01:00:40.560 --> 01:00:42.641
What was the specific date?


01:00:42.761 --> 01:00:44.001
How come?


01:00:44.120 --> 01:00:47.441
Well, it's a long shot,
but l thought maybe...


01:00:47.560 --> 01:00:50.681
if something happened to Eleanor while
she was working here at the Mayflower...


01:00:50.801 --> 01:00:53.001
maybe the security cameras
caught something.


01:00:54.321 --> 01:00:57.161
it was Wednesday, September 22.


01:01:02.120 --> 01:01:04.201
The 22nd.


01:01:10.401 --> 01:01:12.321
it’s not here.


01:01:12.441 --> 01:01:13.401
What?


01:01:13.520 --> 01:01:15.001
it’s missing.


01:01:15.120 --> 01:01:16.881
- Missing?
- Yeah.


01:01:17.001 --> 01:01:19.241
Somebody erased it.


01:01:19.361 --> 01:01:22.441
- Who?
- Well, give me a minute.


01:01:24.001 --> 01:01:27.561
Yeah, last viewed September 24.


01:01:27.680 --> 01:01:29.481
Two days after she disappeared.


01:01:30.200 --> 01:01:32.681
Who was the last person
to view those files?


01:01:33.401 --> 01:01:36.761
Yeah, last viewed,
Henry David Schow.


01:01:36.881 --> 01:01:38.121
Who's that?


01:01:38.240 --> 01:01:42.361
He's the security guard l replaced.
The guy cut himself up and then quit.


01:01:43.441 --> 01:01:45.441
They say he's gone totally Cray.


01:01:45.560 --> 01:01:47.601
All after my sister went missing.


01:01:48.560 --> 01:01:49.761
Can you pick me up?


01:02:04.520 --> 01:02:06.481
Henry Schow?


01:02:07.600 --> 01:02:09.481
Henry, you in there?


01:02:11.961 --> 01:02:15.201
- Henry, is that you?
- Stay away from me.


01:02:15.321 --> 01:02:17.961
Come on.
Henry, open the door.


01:02:22.040 --> 01:02:23.841
l said stay away.


01:02:23.961 --> 01:02:28.041
Henry, we're not here to hurt you.
We just wanna ask a couple questions.


01:02:29.801 --> 01:02:32.001
Don't shut- Henry!


01:02:33.961 --> 01:02:35.401
Who are you?


01:02:35.520 --> 01:02:39.441
l'm your replacement at the Mayflower.
l'm the new night security guard.


01:02:41.401 --> 01:02:42.681
You've seen her then?


01:02:44.481 --> 01:02:45.921
Seen who?


01:02:46.040 --> 01:02:47.361
Her.


01:02:49.720 --> 01:02:51.841
Eleanor.


01:02:51.961 --> 01:02:54.361
What do you know about Eleanor?


01:02:55.001 --> 01:02:56.961
Nothing'. l don't know nothing'.


01:02:57.080 --> 01:02:59.281
Henry, you don't have to lie to us.


01:02:59.401 --> 01:03:03.361
- l'm not lying!
- Yes, you are! What are you hiding?


01:03:04.841 --> 01:03:07.281
She wants to kill me.


01:03:08.680 --> 01:03:11.561
Why does my sister want to kill you?


01:03:12.680 --> 01:03:14.241
Your sister?


01:03:28.560 --> 01:03:32.001
Henry, did you kill my sister?


01:03:35.921 --> 01:03:39.521
No. l don't know
what happened to her.


01:03:42.841 --> 01:03:45.161
But why do you think
she wants to kill you?


01:03:45.281 --> 01:03:47.041
l don't know.


01:03:47.160 --> 01:03:48.921
What about the files?


01:03:49.720 --> 01:03:50.721
What files?


01:03:50.841 --> 01:03:52.801
The digitized security camera files.


01:03:52.921 --> 01:03:54.961
The one from the night
she went missing.


01:03:55.080 --> 01:03:56.961
The ones you erased, Henry.


01:03:59.160 --> 01:04:01.161
l was just following orders!


01:04:01.281 --> 01:04:04.401
Henry, who told you
to erase those files?


01:04:04.520 --> 01:04:07.001
Mr. Landreaux, Keller Landreaux...


01:04:07.120 --> 01:04:09.441
asked me to get rid of 'em,
said it was important.


01:04:09.560 --> 01:04:12.321
- Keller.
- That's when your sister first showed up.


01:04:12.441 --> 01:04:14.321
That night.


01:04:14.441 --> 01:04:17.241
That's when she started
haunting all my mirrors.


01:04:17.361 --> 01:04:19.721
Henry, there's something
you're not telling us.


01:04:19.841 --> 01:04:22.001
l told you everything.


01:04:22.120 --> 01:04:24.241
Henry, now, my sister
went missing the next day.


01:04:24.361 --> 01:04:27.201
And somebody asked you to erase
those security files from the cameras...


01:04:27.321 --> 01:04:29.881
and you didn't think that
was a little bit suspicious?


01:04:30.001 --> 01:04:32.601
No, l didn't.
l didn't think that. l-


01:04:34.520 --> 01:04:36.921
l just didn't wanna know.


01:04:37.040 --> 01:04:40.841
Henry, you need to tell us everything
that happened that night. Everything.


01:04:42.921 --> 01:04:45.281
l just want her to leave me alone.


01:04:45.401 --> 01:04:48.521
She's not goanna stop this
until she gets what she wants.


01:04:48.640 --> 01:04:51.441
Until she gets the truth, Henry!


01:04:51.560 --> 01:04:53.761
l don't know the truth.


01:04:53.881 --> 01:04:58.321
Keller threatened my job, so l just-
l went along with him.


01:04:59.001 --> 01:05:00.881
We were in the basement.


01:05:01.001 --> 01:05:03.481
He said we had to erase the files.


01:05:05.560 --> 01:05:06.921
l'm sorry!


01:05:07.040 --> 01:05:08.921
The basement.


01:05:09.841 --> 01:05:14.201
We have to go back to the Mayflower.
We have to check the basement.


01:05:15.640 --> 01:05:16.801
Basement.


01:05:19.600 --> 01:05:21.281
l'm sorry!


01:06:47.481 --> 01:06:49.441
What is it?


01:06:49.560 --> 01:06:51.441
There's rust on the ground.


01:06:55.680 --> 01:06:58.681
l think it came from that.
It's been moved.


01:07:02.640 --> 01:07:04.641
Give me a hand?


01:07:19.921 --> 01:07:21.761
it’s a crawl space.


01:08:18.440 --> 01:08:19.841
